{"step_index":141,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T09:53:43Z","thinking":"**Defining Core MCP Logic**\n\nI'm currently focused on defining the core logic for the MCP (My Content Platform) engine. Specifically, I'm fleshing out the `mcpEngine.js` file within the `backend/mcp` directory. It looks like it will provide tool definitions and handlers like `get_agency_services` and `get_case_studies`. The first should return active agency service capabilities, and the second, real performance outcomes. I plan to add filters to the `get_case_studies` handler for things like sector and metric.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Set**\n\nI've been adding more handlers to the MCP engine. Now, the logic includes calculating growth ROI, creating leads, and requesting growth audits. I've also implemented lead retrieval and blog post management. Additionally, I've defined new resource entries. I also plan on creating a JSON-RPC 2.0 dispatch helper to be used for Stdio, HTTP and SSE transports.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import crypto from \\\"node:crypto\\\";\\nimport { getSiteContent, saveSiteContent, createId } from \\\"../data/contentStore.js\\\";\\nimport { readFile, writeFile, mkdir, rename } from \\\"node:fs/promises\\\";\\nimport path from \\\"node:path\\\";\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \\\"node:url\\\";\\n\\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\\nconst leadFile = path.join(__dirname, \\\"..\\\", \\\"data\\\", \\\"leads.json\\\");\\nconst leadTempFile = `${leadFile}.tmp`;\\n\\n// Industry benchmarks database for ROI estimation\\nconst INDUSTRY_BENCHMARKS = {\\n  \\\"d2c\\\": { name: \\\"D2C & E-Commerce\\\", avgCpc: 18, convRate: 3.2, roasMultiplier: 4.8, avgTicketSize: 1850 },\\n  \\\"b2b\\\": { name: \\\"B2B SaaS & Enterprise IT\\\", avgCpc: 65, convRate: 4.5, roasMultiplier: 5.4, avgTicketSize: 45000 },\\n  \\\"realestate\\\": { name: \\\"Luxury Real Estate & High-Ticket\\\", avgCpc: 42, convRate: 3.8, roasMultiplier: 6.2, avgTicketSize: 150000 },\\n  \\\"edtech\\\": { name: \\\"EdTech & Career Certifications\\\", avgCpc: 24, convRate: 5.1, roasMultiplier: 4.2, avgTicketSize: 28000 },\\n  \\\"healthcare\\\": { name: \\\"Clinics & Healthcare Networks\\\", avgCpc: 28, convRate: 4.8, roasMultiplier: 5.0, avgTicketSize: 12000 },\\n  \\\"services\\\": { name: \\\"Professional Services & Agencies\\\", avgCpc: 35, convRate: 4.0, roasMultiplier: 4.6, avgTicketSize: 35000 }\\n};\\n\\nasync function readLeads() {\\n  try {\\n    const raw = await readFile(leadFile, \\\"utf8\\\");\\n    return JSON.parse(raw);\\n  } catch (error) {\\n    if (error.code === \\\"ENOENT\\\") return [];\\n    throw error;\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nasync function saveLeads(leads) {\\n  await mkdir(path.dirname(leadFile), { recursive: true });\\n  await writeFile(leadTempFile, JSON.stringify(leads, null, 2));\\n  await rename(leadTempFile, leadFile);\\n}\\n\\n// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n// MCP Tools Schema Declarations\\n// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nexport const MCP_TOOLS = [\\n  {\\n    name: \\\"get_agency_services\\\",\\n \n<truncated 15429 bytes>","Description":"\"Create core Model Context Protocol (MCP) engine for Get Into Feed\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\ashis\\\\OneDrive\\\\Documents\\\\Get into feed\\\\backend\\\\mcp\\\\mcpEngine.js\"","toolAction":"\"Creating mcpEngine.js\"","toolSummary":"\"Create MCP engine\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
